editor, and a man of saintly patience","is_capital_matters":false,"is_wfb_100":false,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_premium_content":true,"table_of_contents":null,"truncated_content":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">T<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">he<\\/span> picture attending this post is of the painting <em>Hungarian Shepherd Boy<\\/em>, by the 19th-century Austrian artist Johann Gualbert Raffalt. It\\u2019s a lovely little work (only eight by ten inches) of oil on board, no? Yes, lovely. And of value, albeit small.<\\/p>\\n<p>Which is why the Nazis wanted it.<\\/p>\\n<p>It has a story \\u2014 \\"<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/magazine\\/2011\\/04\\/04\\/when-nazis-stole-my-painting\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">When the Nazis Stole My Painting<\\/a>\\u201d \\u2014 which proved the most affecting article I have ever read in <span class=\\"small_caps\\">National Review<\\/span>, penned for the April 4, 2011, issue by David Pryce-Jones, NR\\u2019s late senior editor and about as decent and wise a soul as you could ever meet. (On <em><\\/em> ...<\\/p>\\n","right_rail_widget":{"widget_type":"more-from-author","slideshow_widget_title":"Latest Photos","slideshow_widget_post":null,"slideshow_widget_post_title":"","slideshow_widget_categories_exclude":[6068]},"amp_enabled":true,"__type__":"post"},"request":{"type":"singular","object_type":"post","is_premium_content":true,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_metered":true},"schema_ld":"{\\n    \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n    \\"@type\\": \\"NewsArticle\\",\\n    \\"headline\\": \\"Remembering David Pryce-Jones\\",\\n    \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/remembering-david-pryce-jones\\\\\\/\\",\\n    \\"thumbnailUrl\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/i0.wp.com\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/hungarian-shepherd-boy-1.jpg?fit=789%2C460&ssl=1\\",\\n    \\"dateCreated\\": \\"2025