k MusicContains very strong language.Contains discriminatory languageDocumentary revealing the untold stories behind the most controversial music of the 1980s, featuring Frankie Goes to Hollywood, Queen, George Michael, N.W.A, Madonna and others. Duration55 minsFirst shown27 Sep 2025Available for 10 monthsWatchlistAudio DescribedSign LanguageMore Like ThisMore Like This EpisodesThe 80s - Music’s Greatest Decade?Beyond the power ballads. Dylan Jones champions a creative and innovative decade in popMr Blue Sky: The Story of Jeff Lynne and ELOThe pioneer of progressive pop – from the Brum beat scene to huge hits all over the world57 minsGirlbands ForeverGirl power and killer harmonies. A trip through the highs and lows of 90s pop and beyondSince Yesterday: The Untold Story of Scotland's Girl BandsPopstars, punks and pioneers. Defiant trailblazers who rocked a mostly male music world1h 30mWham!: Last Christmas Unwrapped40 years a festive favourite. Andrew, Pepsi and Shirlie revisit Wham!’s winter wonderland59 minsTop of the PopsWith Paul Heaton, Mick Hucknall, Sinitta, The Communards and Swing Out Sister.59 minsErasTrevor Nelson talks all things Bob Marley with his daughter Cedella and grandson Skip.30 minsBoybands ForeverThe flipside of fame – behind the singing and smiles were blood, sweat and tearsLive Aid at 40: When Rock ’n’ Roll Took on the WorldNot just for one day. The creation and legacy of a concert that changed everythingSimon & Garfunkel: The Harmony GameInspiration – and separation. The stormy relationship that created beautiful music1h 11mTOTP2A look back at Eurovision classics, featuring Abba, Lulu, Cliff Richard and Bucks Fizz.59 minsSimple Minds: Everything Is PossibleDaring to dream. The inspirational story of Scotland's biggest band1h 27m\n                                 \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n      \n    \n  	Documentary revealing the untold stories behind the most controversial music of the 1980s, fe