"slug":"thanksgiving","taxonomy":"post_tag","meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]}},"subtitle":"The excellent Norman Rockwell Museum delivers a holiday feast of art.","is_capital_matters":false,"is_wfb_100":false,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_premium_content":true,"table_of_contents":null,"truncated_content":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">Y<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">e <\\/span>olde Arlington, where I live in southwestern Vermont, has, for a town of fewer than 2,500 people, abundant claims to fame. Many of the Green Mountain Boys lived here. Arlington was for a time capital of the Vermont Republic, taking it international, though with a population then in the hundreds, it must have been the world\\u2019s smallest. Robert Frost knew Arlington well, coaxed to live in neighboring Shaftsbury by Dorothy Canfield Fisher, Arlington\\u2019s culture queen, a Pulitzer-finalist writer, the pioneer in the Montessori method in America, and an assiduous networker. And then there\\u2019s Norman Rockwell (1894\\u20131978).<\\/p>\\n<p>Rockwell, his wife, Mary, <em><\\/em> ...<\\/p>\\n","right_rail_widget":{"widget_type":"more-from-author","slideshow_widget_title":"Latest Photos","slideshow_widget_post":null,"slideshow_widget_post_title":"","slideshow_widget_categories_exclude":[6068]},"amp_enabled":true,"__type__":"post"},"request":{"type":"singular","object_type":"post","is_premium_content":true,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_metered":true},"schema_ld":"{\\n    \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n    \\"@type\\": \\"NewsArticle\\",\\n    \\"headline\\": \\"A Norman Rockwell Thanksgiving\\",\\n    \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/a-norman-rockwell-thanksgiving\\\\\\/\\",\\n    \\"thumbnailUrl\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/i0.wp.com\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/norman-rockwell.jpg?fit=789%2C460&ssl=1\\",\\n    \\"dateCreated\\": \\"2025-11-2