y","taxonomy":"post_tag","meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]}},"subtitle":"Andrew Ross Sorkin\\u2019s <i>1929<\\/i> is an artful yet flawed reprise of John Kenneth Galbraith\\u2019s book on the same topic.","is_capital_matters":true,"is_wfb_100":false,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_premium_content":true,"table_of_contents":null,"truncated_content":"<p><span class=\\"small_caps\\"><span class=\\"drop\\">B<\\/span>ack<\\/span> in 1999, Bill Buckley <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=uFBdraRvxxk\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">interviewed<\\/a> the economist John Kenneth Galbraith on <em>Firing Line<\\/em>. The gents\\u2019 topic was historic figures. Around 24 minutes in, Buckley got to President Franklin Roosevelt. Galbraith, then 90, turned nostalgic.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cOf my generation, there was no figure like Franklin Delano Roosevelt. And I still wake up in the morning and say, \\u2018Well, Galbraith, you\\u2019re still a New Dealer.\\u2019\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>Certainly. But do the rest of us have to be?<\\/p>\\n<p>Apparently, yes. For \\u201cWe are all New Dealers now\\u201d is likewise a conclusion of <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.amazon.com\\/1929-Inside-Greatest-History-Shattered\\/dp\\/0593296966\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Andrew Ross Sorkin\\u2019s <em>1929<\\/em><\\/a>, an artful reprise of Galbraith\\u2019s book on the same topic, <em><a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.amazon.com\\/Great-Crash-1929-Kenneth-Galbraith\\/dp\\/0547248164\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">The Great <\\/a><\\/em> ...<\\/p>\\n","right_rail_widget":{"widget_type":"more-from-author","slideshow_widget_title":"Latest Photos","slideshow_widget_post":null,"slideshow_widget_post_title":"","slideshow_widget_categories_exclude":[6068]},"amp_enabled":true,"__type__":"post"},"request":{"type":"singular","object_type":"post","is_premium_content":true,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_metered":true},"schema_ld":"{\\n    \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n    \\"@type\\": \\"NewsArticle\\",\\n    \\"headline\\": \\"Sorkin Rounds Up the Usual Suspects\\",\\n    \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/sorkin-rounds-up-the-usual-suspects\\\\\\/\\",\\n    \\"thumbnailUrl\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/i0.wp.com\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/1929-stock-market-crash.jpg?fit=789%2C460&ssl=1\\",\\n    \\"dateCreated\\": \\"2025-11-27T06:30:57-05:00\\",\\n    \\"datePublished\\": \\"2025-11-27T06:30:57-05:00\\",\\n    \\"dateModified\\": \\"2025-11-27T00:44:20-05:00\\",\\n    \\"articleSection\\": [\\n        \\"articles\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"creator\\": [\\n        \\"Amity Shlaes\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"author\\": [\\n        \\"Amity Shlaes\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"keywords\\": [\\n        \\"topic: Capital Matters\\",\\n        \\"topic: History\\",\\n        \\"topic: The Forgotten Book\\",\\n        \\"American History\\",\\n        \\"NRPLUS Member Articles\\",\\n        \\"section: Article\\",\\n        \\"Premium Content\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"metadata\\": {\\n        \\"wordcount\\": 1873,\\n        \\"postType\\": \\"post\\",\\n        \\"post_id\\": 1897693,\\n        \\"hide_from_widgets\\": false\\n    },\\n    \\"isAccessibleForFree\\": \\"\\",\\n    \\"hasPart\\": [],\\n    \\"publisher\\": {\\n        \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n        \\"@type\\": \\"Organization\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"National Review\\",\\n        \\"logo\\": {\\n            \\"@type\\": \\"ImageObject\\",\\n            \\"name\\": \\"National Review\\",\\n            \\"width\\": \\"360\\",\\n            \\"height\\": \\"180\\",\\n            \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/themes\\\\\\/national-review\\\\\\/static\\\\\\/images\\\\\\/logo.png\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"