"modified_gmt":"2025-11-26T06:12:23","slug":"rfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/rfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines\\/","title":{"rendered":"RFK Jr. Takes a Dangerous Step on Vaccines"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">H<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">ealth and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr.<\\/span>, who has a long history of raising unwarranted skepticism about vaccines, took a dangerous step last week when he ordered the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention to revise its message that vaccines do not cause autism.<\\/p>\\n<Connatix preset=\\"loggedOut\\"><\\/Connatix>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-1\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-large\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>Under RFK Jr.\\u2019s guidance, the CDC\\u00a0<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.cdc.gov\\/vaccine-safety\\/about\\/autism.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">website<\\/a>, which previously debunked the unfounded theories about the link, now has an asterisk next to the heading \\u201cVaccines do not cause Autism.\\u201d The description below says the statement\\u00a0\\u201cis not an evidence-based claim. Scientific studies have not ruled out the possibility that infant vaccines contribute to the development of autism. However, this statement has historically been disseminated by the CDC and other federal health agencies within HHS to prevent vaccine hesitancy.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>In an\\u00a0<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nytimes.com\\/2025\\/11\\/21\\/us\\/politics\\/rfk-jr-cdc-vaccines-autism-website.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">interview<\\/a>\\u00a0with the\\u00a0<em>New York Times<\\/em>\\u00a0about the change, RFK Jr. said that while large studies have found no link between the measles, mumps, and rubella vaccine and autism, there had not been large studies of the links with other vaccines to completely rule out any relationship. Yet it wouldn\\u2019t make sense for a health agency to set the bar at proving a negative and requiring a massive-scale study to debunk every cockamamie theory for which there is no scientific support. As one doctor quoted in the\\u00a0<em>Times<\\/em>\\u00a0article quipped, \\u201cYou can\\u2019t prove that Coca-Cola doesn\\u2019t cause autism either.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>Proponents of the vaccines-cause-autism theory have either relied on discredited research, such as Andrew Wakefield\\u2019s retracted 1998 study, or made the classic mistake of mixing up correlation and causation. Conspiracy theorists, for instance, will point to cases of young children getting diagnosed with autism after receiving shots as evidence of something rather than the simple fact that autism signs manifest themselves in the early years, which is around the same time that children get vaccinated. Much of the statistical rise in autism that has been observed over the past several decades, and that skeptics blame on vaccines, can be attributed to an increasing awareness of autism, a change in the diagnosis criteria, and more-advanced screening tools. While there may be other causes that researchers are investigating, there is no evidence to focus on vaccines, which have incredible health benefits.<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-small\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>Senator Bill Cassidy was\\u00a0<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/SenBillCassidy\\/status\\/1991599014270365829\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">critical<\\/a> of the CDC website decision, citing his experience as a doctor and noting deaths of children who had died of vaccine-preventable diseases. But Cassidy, who chairs the Senate Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee, provided a crucial vote to confirm RFK Jr. Explaining his support in a February floor speech, Cassidy <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.cassidy.senate.gov\\/newsroom\\/press-releases\\/cassidy-delivers-floor-speech-in-support-of-rfk-jr-to-be-hhs-secretary\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">said<\\/a> that the nominee had committed to him that the \\u201cCDC will not remove statements on their website pointing out that vaccines do not cause autism.\\u201d Given RFK Jr.&#8217;s decades of \\u201cjust asking questions\\u201d about the link between vaccines and autism, it\\u2019s hard to believe that an intelligent lawmaker like Cassidy was so easily deceived. More likely, Cassidy was concerned about drawing Trump\\u2019s ire ahead of his daunting 2026 reelection bid.<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-2\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit><TopStories variant=\\"default\\"><\\/TopStories>\\n<p>Unfortunately, RFK Jr. was confirmed, and now that he is in a position of authority,\\u00a0<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.cdc.gov\\/measles\\/data-research\\/index.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">reckless<\\/a>\\u00a0actions could have real-world consequences as the efficacy of vaccines ultimately relies on having a critical mass of the population vaccinated, denying viruses enough hosts to spread sufficiently. Already, in 2025, the U.S. has seen the\\u00a0<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.cdc.gov\\/measles\\/data-research\\/index.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">most measles cases since 1992<\\/a> \\u2014 with the number spiking sixfold since 2024. Whatever caveats RFK Jr. may try to give in interviews to claim that he isn\\u2019t totally anti-vaccine, the clear signal being sent by the nation\\u2019s top health official is that those on the fence about vaccinating their children should take a pause.<\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Changing the CDC website to suggest a link between vaccines and autism could have devastating real-world consequences. <\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"author":149,"featured_media":1871789,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"hide-more-from-author":false,"disable-player":false,"disable-wfb-100-badge":false,"disable-wfb-100-archive-widget":false,"disable-wfb-100-legacy-widget":false,"hide_top_stories":false,"headline_variations":[],"coral_asset_id":"","_cr_original_post":"","_cr_replace_post_id":"","_cr_replacing_post_id":"","_links_to":"","_links_to_type":0,"original-print-title":"","hide-nrplus":"1","social":{"tweet":"","share-chart":false},"footnotes":""},"categories":[5882,1389],"tags":[6275,5445,9457,4632],"section":[615],"coauthors":[170],"class_list":["post-1897237","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-health-care","category-politics-policy","tag-cdc","tag-department-of-health-and-human-services","tag-robert-f-kennedy-jr","tag-vaccines","section-article"],"share_buttons":{"facebook":{"title":"Share on Facebook","href":"https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/sharer\\/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Frfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines%2F"},"twitter":{"title":"Share on Twitter","href":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/intent\\/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Frfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines%2F&text=RFK%20Jr.%20Takes%20a%20Dangerous%20Step%20on%20Vaccines"},"flipboard":{"title":"Share on Flipboard","href":"https:\\/\\/share.flipboard.com\\/bookmarklet\\/popout?v=2&title=RFK%20Jr.%20Takes%20a%20Dangerous%20Step%20on%20Vaccines&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Frfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines%2F&utm_campaign=tools&utm_medium=article-share&utm_source=https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/"},"whatsapp":{"title":"Share on WhatsApp","href":"https:\\/\\/wa.me\\/?text=RFK%20Jr.%20Takes%20a%20Dangerous%20Step%20on%20Vaccines%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Frfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines%2F"},"copylink":{"title":"Copy Link","href":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/rfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines\\/"},"email":{"title":"Email this article","href":"mailto:?body=RFK Jr. Takes a Dangerous Step on Vaccines https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/rfk-jr-takes-a-dangerous-step-on-vaccines\\/"},"printer":{"title":"Print this article","href":""}},"authors":[{"include_full":false,"id":145605,"description":"<p>The Editors comprise the senior editorial staff of the <span style=\\"font-variant: small-caps\\">National Review<\\/span> magazine and website.<\\/p>","display_name":"The Editors","email":"editors@nationalreview.com","feed_url":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/author\\/feed\\/","first_name":"The","full_description":"","href":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/author\\/the-editors\\/","image":"<img width=\\"138\\" height=\\"138\\" src=\\"https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2017\\/09\\/Untitled-design-81.png?resize=138%2C138&amp;ssl=1\\" class=\\"attachment-avatar size-avatar\\" alt=\\"\\" decoding=\\"async\\" loading=\\"lazy\\" \\/>","image_url":"https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2017\\/09\\/Untitled-design-81.png?resize=138%2C138&ssl=1","last_name":"Editors","slug":"the-editors","tagline":"","twitter":""}],"byline":"<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/author\\/the-editors\\/\\" title=\\"Posts by The Editors\\" class=\\"author article-header__meta-author\\" rel=\\"author\\" data-author-id=\\"145605\\"  aria-haspopup=\\"true\\">The Editors<\\/a>","blog_post_content":null,"curation_below_article":{"revcontent":true,"upper":[],"zergnet":false,"lower":{"posts":[{"id":1897693,"date":"2025-11-27T06:30:57","type":"post","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/sorkin-rounds-up-the-usual-suspects\\/","title":{"rendered":"Sorkin Rounds Up the Usual Suspects"},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Andrew Ross Sorkin\\u2019s <i