t":null,"primary_category":{"id":7508,"count":1399,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/history\\/","name":"History","slug":"history","taxonomy":"category","parent":0,"meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]},"is_capital_matters_archive":false,"specific_term_link":"<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/history\\/\\" class=\\"underline\\">History<\\/a>"},"primary_section":{"id":615,"count":86346,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/article\\/","name":"Article","slug":"article","taxonomy":"section","parent":0,"meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]},"is_capital_matters_archive":false},"primary_tag":{"id":2849,"count":127,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/tag\\/thanksgiving\\/","name":"Thanksgiving","slug":"thanksgiving","taxonomy":"post_tag","meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]}},"subtitle":"Were the pilgrims really \\u2018ethno-nationalists\\u2019?","is_capital_matters":false,"is_wfb_100":false,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_premium_content":true,"table_of_contents":null,"truncated_content":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">T<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\"><em>he Federalist<\\/em><\\/span>\\u2019s John Daniel Davidson recently advanced a provocative theory, one summarized in the headline of his piece: \\u201c<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/thefederalist.com\\/2025\\/11\\/26\\/the-pilgrims-were-english-ethno-nationalists\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">The Pilgrims Were English Ethno-Nationalists<\\/a>.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>According to Davidson, the popular history you\\u2019ve learned about colonial New England is, if not inaccurate, at least \\u201cincomplete.\\u201d Yes, the early 17th century Puritans who fled from England were escaping religious persecution. But in Holland and America, the Congregationalist diaspora established for themselves a \\u201c<em>self-consciously<\\/em> English\\u201d \\u2014 indeed even \\u201c<em>hyper<\\/em>-English\\u201d \\u2014 social covenant. Davidson cites in support of this contention Cotton Mather\\u2019s trepidation over the prospect of \\u201cCriolian degeneracy\\u201d descending upon Massachusetts Bay. The colonists never gave <em><\\/em> ...<\\/p>\\n","right_rail_widget":{"widget_type":"more-from-author","slideshow_widget_title":"Latest Photos","slideshow_widget_post":null,"slideshow_widget_post_title":"","slideshow_widget_categories_exclude":[6068]},"amp_enabled":true,"__type__":"post"},"request":{"type":"singular","object_type":"post","is_premium_content":true,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_metered":true},"schema_ld":"{\\n    \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n    \\"@type\\": \\"NewsArticle\\",\\n    \\"headline\\": \\"A Misreading of the Puritans\\",\\n    \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/a-misreading-of-the-puritans\\\\\\/\\",\\n    \\"thumbnailUrl\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/i0.wp.com\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/landing-pilgrims.jpg?fit=789%2C460&ssl=1\\",\\n    \\"dateCreated\\": \\"2025-11-27T06:30:06-05:00\\",\\n    \\"datePublished\\": \\"2025-11-27T06:30:06-05:00\\",\\n    \\"dateModified\\": \\"2025-11-27T06:10:44-05:00\\",\\n    \\"articleSection\\": [\\n        \\"articles\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"creator\\": [\\n        \\"Noah Rothman\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"author\\": [\\n        \\"Noah Rothman\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"keywords\\": [\\n        \\"topic: Culture\\",\\n        \\"topic: History\\",\\n        \\"topic: Religion\\",\\n        \\"American History\\",\\n        \\"Founding Fathers\\",\\n        \\"Love of Country\\",\\n        \\"NRPLUS Member Articles\\",\\n        \\"Thanksgiving\\",\\n        \\"section: Article\\",\\n        \\"Premium Content\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"metadata\\": {\\n        \\"wordcount\\": 1277,\\n        \\"postType\\": \\"post\\",\\n        \\"post_id\\": 1897704,\\n        \\"hide_from_widgets\\