paywalls or content meters, ad-light reading, and community perks.<\\/p>\\n","button":"GET STARTED","button_link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe"},"timestamp":"<time class=\\"article-header__meta-pubdate separator\\" datetime=\\"2025-11-26T14:25:47-05:00\\" title=\\"November 26, 2025 2:25 PM\\">November 26, 2025 2:25 PM<\\/time>","queried_object":{"id":1897503,"date":"2025-11-26T14:25:47","date_gmt":"2025-11-26T19:25:47","guid":{"rendered":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/?p=1897503"},"modified":"2025-11-26T15:47:17","modified_gmt":"2025-11-26T20:47:17","slug":"young-women-are-sitting-ducks-under-progressive-rule","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/young-women-are-sitting-ducks-under-progressive-rule\\/","title":{"rendered":"Young Women Are Sitting Ducks Under Progressive Rule"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">A<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">nother <\\/span>innocent, beautiful young woman was viciously attacked by a career criminal on public transportation, this time in Chicago. Twenty-six-year-old Bethany MaGee was set on fire and critically injured by a mentally ill menace who reportedly had \\u2014 prepare to be appalled \\u2014 72 prior arrests. What\\u2019s next?<\\/p>\\n<Connatix preset=\\"loggedOut\\"><\\/Connatix>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-1\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-large\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>The attack comes just three months after the horror of Ukrainian refugee Iryna Zarutska\\u2019s brutal murder on North Carolina public transit, allegedly by Decarlos Brown Jr., who had been arrested and institutionalized <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/corner\\/hes-the-killer-not-the-victim\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">more than a dozen times<\\/a>. The details of the Chicago attack are tragically similar: On November 17, MaGee was quietly reading on her phone on the Blue Line train when a man <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/cwbchicago.com\\/2025\\/11\\/prosecutor-warned-judge-before-release-of-man-now-accused-in-cta-fire-attack-transcripts.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">doused<\\/a> her body with gasoline. She tried to run away, but the maniac chased her down, with the bottle already on fire, and set her ablaze. The young woman was engulfed in flames but somehow escaped the train before collapsing on the platform.<\\/p>\\n<p>Thankfully, not every person taking public transit these days is so desensitized or apathetic to violence that they\\u2019d rather film it or stare sheepishly (though, in their defense, there\\u2019s little incentive to intervene given how Daniel Penny was <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/corner\\/do-not-forget-daniel-pennys-tormentors\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">villainized<\\/a> by New York City prosecutor Alvin Bragg and the media). Bystanders helped MaGee, before she was rushed to the hospital in critical condition.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cMy responsibility is to build the safest, most affordable city in America,\\u201d Democratic Chicago Mayor Brandon Johnson said at a recent <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/EricLDaugh\\/status\\/1991935165803983287?s=20\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">press briefing<\\/a>. \\u201cThe investments we are making are certainly moving us in that direction. This is an isolated incident, I mean, I don\\u2019t see this as some sort of trend.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-small\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-2\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit><TopStories variant=\\"default\\"><\\/TopStories>\\n<p>Yet the city\\u2019s habitual release of suspect Lawrence Reed &#8212; <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/cwbchicago.com\\/2025\\/11\\/prosecutor-warned-judge-before-release-of-man-now-accused-in-cta-fire-attack-transcripts.html\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">who at one point reportedly was being held at a psychiatric hospital<\\/a> &#8212; back onto the streets does constitute a trend, at a minimum. Even three arrests by Chicago police would have been a trend. But <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/abcnews.go.com\\/US\\/judge-orders-suspect-remain-detained-after-woman-set\\/story?id=127754639#:~:text=Reed%20has%20been%20arrested%20by,2016%2C%20according%20to%20the%20filing.\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">72 arrests<\\/a>? That feels like a government conspiracy to terrorize citizens. The criminal justice philosophy of Chicago\\u2019s leaders is incompatible with American civil society, which must foster confidence in public safety.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cWe cannot incarcerate our way out of violence,\\u201d Johnson <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/america\\/status\\/1993377550991851905?s=20\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">said<\\/a>\\u00a0in a separate press conference recently. \\u201cIt is racist, it is immoral, it is unholy, it is not the way to drive violence down.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>We\\u2019ve heard this argument before from feckless city officials, and it is abject nonsense &#8212; and dangerous. Incarceration removes individuals who\\u2019ve broken the social contract by menacing other people. In prison, they pay a penalty for their crimes and are no longer a threat to the law-abiding public.<\\/p>\\n<Connatix preset=\\"legacy\\"><\\/Connatix>\\n<p>And since Johnson wants to open that can of worms, the black incarceration rate is overwhelmingly related to rates of crime involving black perpetrators. In 2005, the <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/manhattan.institute\\/article\\/high-incarceration-rate-of-blacks-is-function-of-crime-not-racism\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">black homicide rate<\\/a> was more than seven times higher than that of whites and Hispanics combined, according to the federal Bureau of Justice Statistics.<\\/p>\\n<p>To explain this discrepancy, Johnson and his radical criminal-justice-reform peers will argue that the whole system is rigged \\u2014 that police, prosecutors, and judges apply bias to black people accused of crimes. This has served as the justification for rogue district attorneys to impose soft-on-crime policies, such as bail reform, that lower the bar for letting recidivist criminals prowl about the streets again.<\\/p>\\n<p>After a career felon set MaGee on fire, Fox News asked a <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/RedWave_Press\\/status\\/1993310388025213000?s=20\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">commuter<\\/a> for her reaction.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cWere you aware that the individual that allegedly committed this crime was a career offender and had been arrested over 40 times?\\u201d Fox asked the woman, who is black.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cI saw it on the news,\\u201d she said. \\u201cThe guy should have been in jail at some point. I mean, he should have been in jail and not able to move. I mean, this guy was carrying an accelerant around.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>Fox asked: \\u201cDid you know that [Chicago] Mayor Brandon Johnson said, \\u2018Oh, this was just an isolated incident\\u2019? How does that make you feel?\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-3-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-large\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit><MoreFromAuthor desktop=\\"true\\" variant=\\"default\\"><\\/MoreFromAuthor><MoreInTag variant=\\"default\\"><\\/MoreInTag>\\n<p>\\u201cThat he doesn\\u2019t care,\\u201d she replied. \\u201cThat he blows it off. That he doesn\\u2019t think he has to do anything about it. That\\u2019s not his job.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-3-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-3\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-4-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-4\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>Johnson\\u2019s callous dismissal of MaGee\\u2019s experience, which likely will leave her permanently scarred physically and emotionally, feels personal to a lot of women who know they\\u2019d be just as easy targets. I\\u2019m only a year older than MaGee, and I live in deep-blue New York City where I often feel like a sitting duck. Though Mayor-Elect Zohran Mamdani\\u2019s retention of top cop Jessica Tisch gives me some solace, I shudder at the thought of the city\\u2019s subways teeming with even more potentially volatile individuals \\u2014 as the socialist candidate all but promised with his proposal to <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/nypost.com\\/2025\\/05\\/04\\/opinion\\/nyc-subway-is-no-homeless-shelter-zohran-mamdani-cant-you-pretend-to-care-about-the-city\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">convert<\\/a> empty MTA retail spaces into de facto homeless shelters.<\\/p>\\n<p>In a huge step backward, Mamdani just announced that he appointed to his transition team a radical professor who is a <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/blogs.law.columbia.edu\\/abolition1313\\/alex-s-vitale-abolitionist-origins\\/?cn-reloaded=1\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">documented prison abolitionist<\\/a>. Alex Vitale said <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/thestustustudio\\/status\\/1993111704629395961?s=20\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">on a call<\\/a> with the Democratic Socialists of America that cops are \\u201cthe natural enemy of the working class.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>Interesting, because the working class are the ones being victimized when the law enforcement system fails. Zarutska was on her way home from her pizza parlor job when she was stabbed to death. MaGee was taking a commuter train when she became the prey of a <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/docs.google.com\\/document\\/d\\/10sxFvRORSfv55FJYCkKBoZDGyvh9atAO_pQ1QmjD6sk\\/edit?tab=t.0\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">pyro<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n<p>Mamdani, Johnson, and their fellow travelers are making life hell for working people. Their approach to criminal justice is what\\u2019s immoral and unholy &#8212; and, for young women, terrifying.<\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Another public-transit attack by a deranged recidivist, this time in Chicago. <\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"author":155,"featured_media":1897526,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"hide-more-from-author":false,"disable-player":false,"disable-wfb-100-badge":false,"disable-wfb-100-archive-widget":false,"disable-wfb-100-legacy-widget":false,"hide_top_stories":false,"headline_variations":[],"coral_asset_id":"","_cr_original_post":"","_cr_replace_post_id":"","_cr_replacing_post_id":"","_links_to":"","_links_to_type":0,"original-print-title":"","hide-nrplus":"1","social":{"tweet":"","share-chart":false},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1393,1389],"tags":[2428,2982,7839,5530,7109,3563,3525],"section":[615],"coauthors":[8284],"class_list":["post-1897503","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-law-the-courts","category-politics-policy","tag-chicago","tag-crime","tag-democrats","tag-law-enforcement","tag-nrplus-member-articles","tag-progressives","tag-the-left","section-article"],"share_buttons":{"facebook":{"title":"Share on Facebook","href":"https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/sharer\\/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Fyoung-women-are-sitting-ducks-under-progressive-rule%2F"},"twitter":{"title":"Share on Twitter","href":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/intent\\/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Fyoung-women-are-sitting-ducks-under-progressive-rule%2F&text=Young%20Women%20Are%20Sitting%20Ducks%20Under%20Progressive%20Rule"},"flipboard":{"title":"Share on Flipboard","href":"https:\\/\\/share.flipboard.com\\/bookmarklet\\/popout?v=2&title=Young%20Women%20Are%20Sitting%20Ducks%20Under%20Progressive%20Rule&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Fyoung-women-are-sitting-ducks-under-progressive-rule%2F&utm_