resses the League of United Latin American Citizens Nevada Presidential Town Hall in Las Vegas, Nev., February 13, 2020.\\" loading=\\"lazy\\" sizes=\\"auto, (max-width: 252px) 100vw, 252px\\" decoding=\\"async\\" srcset=\\"https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/11\\/tom-steyer-2.jpg?resize=252%2C141&amp;ssl=1 252w, https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/11\\/tom-steyer-2.jpg?resize=160%2C90&amp;ssl=1 160w, https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/11\\/tom-steyer-2.jpg?resize=50%2C29&amp;ssl=1 50w, https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/11\\/tom-steyer-2.jpg?zoom=2&amp;resize=252%2C141&amp;ssl=1 504w\\" \\/>"},"source_url":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/11\\/tom-steyer-2.jpg"},"featured_video":{"url":"","title":"","click_url":"","image_url":""},"issue":null,"series":null,"host":null,"primary_category":{"id":1389,"count":104618,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/politics-policy\\/","name":"Politics &amp; Policy","slug":"politics-policy","taxonomy":"category","parent":0,"meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]},"is_capital_matters_archive":false,"specific_term_link":"<a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/politics-policy\\/\\" class=\\"underline\\">Politics &amp; Policy<\\/a>"},"primary_section":{"id":615,"count":86346,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/article\\/","name":"Article","slug":"article","taxonomy":"section","parent":0,"meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]},"is_capital_matters_archive":false},"primary_tag":{"id":7363,"count":5,"description":"","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/tag\\/tom-steyer\\/","name":"Tom Steyer","slug":"tom-steyer","taxonomy":"post_tag","meta":{"blog-section":false,"section-blog-ads":[]}},"subtitle":"Tom Steyer wants to turn the state further to the left.","is_capital_matters":false,"is_wfb_100":false,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_premium_content":true,"table_of_contents":null,"truncated_content":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">M<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">ichael Bloomberg,<\\/span> the billionaire media mogul and former New York City mayor, became infamous for spending more than $1 billion on his 2020 campaign for the Democratic presidential nomination. He dropped out having won only one party delegate.<\\/p>\\n<p>There was another billionaire who went bust in the 2020 Democratic primaries. California hedge fund founder Tom Steyer spent $345 million of his own money, $4,600 for every vote he received, and won no delegates.<\\/p>\\n<p>Bloomberg has, wisely, retired to run his philanthropic empire. But the 68-year-old Steyer is still burning with political ambition and fanaticism over the perils of climate change. This fall, <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/TomSteyer\\/status\\/1991145045337284945?s=20%5d(https:\\/\\/x.com\\/TomSteyer\\/status\\/1991145045337284945?s=20)\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\"><\\/a> ...<\\/p>\\n","right_rail_widget":{"widget_type":"more-from-author","slideshow_widget_title":"Latest Photos","slideshow_widget_post":null,"slideshow_widget_post_title":"","slideshow_widget_categories_exclude":[6068]},"amp_enabled":true,"__type__":"post"},"request":{"type":"singular","object_type":"post","is_premium_content":true,"is_magazine_article":false,"is_metered":true},"schema_ld":"{\\n    \\"@context\\": \\"http:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\",\\n    \\"@type\\": \\"NewsArticle\\",\\n    \\"headline\\": \\"Can a California Billionaire Spend His Way into the Governor\\\\u2019s Mansion?\\",\\n    \\"url\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\/11\\\\\\/can-a-california-billionaire-spend-his-way-into-the-governors-mansion\\\\\\/\\",\\n    \\"thumbnailUrl\\": \\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/i0.wp.com\\\\\\/www.nationalreview.com\\\\\\/wp-content\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/2025\\\\\\