\/2024\\/08\\/coffee_brass_icon-NLblock.png?fit=253%2C202&amp;ssl=1\\" class=\\"attachment-large size-large\\" alt=\\"\\" loading=\\"lazy\\" sizes=\\"auto, (max-width: 253px) 100vw, 253px\\" decoding=\\"async\\" srcset=\\"https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/08\\/coffee_brass_icon-NLblock.png?w=253&amp;ssl=1 253w, https:\\/\\/i0.wp.com\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/08\\/coffee_brass_icon-NLblock.png?resize=50%2C40&amp;ssl=1 50w\\" \\/>"},"source_url":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/08\\/coffee_brass_icon-NLblock.png"},"image_max_width_desktop":"175px","image_max_width_mobile":"150px","image_padding_desktop":"15px","image_padding_mobile":"10px"},"next_up":{"id":1896610,"link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/lets-hope-the-russia-ukraine-peace-proposal-improves\\/","title":{"rendered":"Let\\u2019s Hope the Russia\\u2013Ukraine Peace Proposal Improves"},"cta_label":"Next Article"},"nrplus_cta":{"enabled":false,"title":"Something to Consider","description":"<p>If you enjoyed this article, we have a proposition for you:\\u00a0<a href=\\"http:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\" data-saferedirecturl=\\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/url?q=http:\\/\\/preprod.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1689865862247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw310hE1-m3o_FFzVsjI_hJA\\">Join NRPLUS<\\/a>. Members get all of our content (including the magazine), no paywalls or content meters, an advertising-minimal experience, and unique access to our writers and editors (through conference calls, social media groups, and more). And importantly, NRPLUS members help keep NR going.<\\/p>\\n<div><\\/div>\\n","description_mobile":"<p>If you enjoyed this article, we have a proposition for you:\\u00a0<a href=\\"http:\\/\\/preprod.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\" data-saferedirecturl=\\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/url?q=http:\\/\\/preprod.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1689865862247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw310hE1-m3o_FFzVsjI_hJA\\">Join NRPLUS<\\/a>. Members get all of our content, no paywalls or content meters, ad-light reading, and community perks.<\\/p>\\n","button":"GET STARTED","button_link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/subscribe"},"timestamp":"<time class=\\"article-header__meta-pubdate separator\\" datetime=\\"2025-11-25T06:30:31-05:00\\" title=\\"November 25, 2025 6:30 AM\\">November 25, 2025 6:30 AM<\\/time>","queried_object":{"id":1896973,"date":"2025-11-25T06:30:31","date_gmt":"2025-11-25T11:30:31","guid":{"rendered":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/?p=1896973"},"modified":"2025-11-25T00:35:20","modified_gmt":"2025-11-25T05:35:20","slug":"trumps-terrorist-designation-of-muslim-brotherhood-sends-right-message","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/2025\\/11\\/trumps-terrorist-designation-of-muslim-brotherhood-sends-right-message\\/","title":{"rendered":"Trump\\u2019s Terrorist Designation of Muslim Brotherhood Sends Right Message"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span class=\\"drop\\">T<\\/span><span class=\\"small_caps\\">he<\\/span> Trump administration has <a href=\\"https:\\/\\/www.whitehouse.gov\\/presidential-actions\\/2025\\/11\\/designation-of-certain-muslim-brotherhood-chapters-as-foreign-terrorist-organizations-and-specially-designated-global-terrorists\\/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">announced<\\/a>\\u00a0a plan to designate various subdivisions of the Muslim Brotherhood as foreign terrorist organizations and specially designated global terrorists, moves that enable our government to take criminal enforcement actions and seize assets. While it\\u2019s not a sweeping designation of the Brotherhood itself, which would be legally and diplomatically fraught, the announcement is a welcome development that conveys the right message about the organization.<\\/p>\\n<Connatix preset=\\"loggedOut\\"><\\/Connatix>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-1\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-1-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-large\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>The Muslim Brotherhood (<em>Jama\\u2019at al-Ikhwan al Muslimun<\\/em>) is the most consequential Islamist movement in modern history. Since its founding in Cairo by Hassan al-Banna in the late 1920s, it has spawned a global network of organizations, including jihadist organizations &#8212; Hamas, most notoriously &#8212; that are united in their sharia-supremacist ideology, which is virulent in its hostility to Western liberalism and its Jew hatred.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Brotherhood has a violent history. Its \\u201cspecial apparatus\\u201d in Egypt murdered Prime Minister Nukrashi Pasha in 1948 and thereafter attempted to murder Prime Minister Gamal Abdel Nasser. In 1981, splinter groups inspired by Brotherhood ideology murdered President Anwar Sadat. By 1987, abetted by Brotherhood tentacles in the United States, Hamas was established as the Brotherhood\\u2019s Palestinian branch. From the first intifada through the still-ongoing war in Gaza, support for the jihad against Israel &#8212; material and financial, through recruitment, rhetoric, and indoctrination &#8212; has been a top priority of Brotherhood-linked organizations throughout the world.<\\/p>\\n<p>Many major Islamist organizations in the United States have Brotherhood roots. That undeniable fact was proven in the Bush 43\\u2013era prosecution of the Holy Land Foundation for Relief and Development. The HLF was an umbrella organization for the material and rhetorical support of Hamas.<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-small\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-2-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-2\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit><TopStories variant=\\"default\\"><\\/TopStories>\\n<p>Many U.S.-based Islamist organizations were shown to have collaborative ties, including the Council on American-Islamic Relations (CAIR), the Islamic Society of North America (developed out of the Muslim Students Association, which has hundreds of chapters across our country), and the North American Islamic Trust (a pivotal player in the acquisition of mosques). It is not a mystery why, after Hamas\\u2019s October 7 atrocities, there was a groundswell of pro-Hamas agitation and a surge in antisemitic incidents.<\\/p>\\n<p>In a sense, Monday\\u2019s designation announcement is unfinished business from the first Trump administration. For years, the potential designation of the Brotherhood has been the subject of legislative proposals, led by Senator Ted Cruz (R., Texas), among others.<\\/p>\\n<p>If nothing else, the Trump announcement is a worthy corrective to the Obama administration\\u2019s delusional portrayal of the Brotherhood, in the words of then\\u2013Director of National Intelligence James Clapper, as a \\u201clargely secular\\u201d group that \\u201chas eschewed violence and decried al-Qaeda as a perversion of Islam.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>To be sure, such unabashed terrorist forces as al-Qaeda, Egyptian Islamic Jihad, and ISIS occasionally exhibit impatience with the Brotherhood\\u2019s Fabian, multifaceted approach to the Islamist mission &#8212; an approach that favors infiltration and co-option of a targeted society\\u2019s institutions, rather than violent attacks, especially in the West. Nevertheless, these jihadist organizations have unmistakable Brotherhood roots; and for its part, the Brotherhood leverages the threat of jihadist violence in pursuing their common agenda.<\\/p>\\n<Connatix preset=\\"legacy\\"><\\/Connatix>\\n<p>In short, there is nothing secular or moderate about the Brotherhood whose credo, to this day, remains: \\u201cAllah is our objective, the Prophet is our leader, the Quran is our law, jihad is our way, and dying in the way of Allah is our highest hope.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>That said, the designation issue is complicated.<\\/p>\\n<p>As it currently exists, the Brotherhood is amorphous. Technically speaking, it still has vestiges of an organizational hierarchy in Cairo &#8212; nominally, Mohammed Badie has been its \\u201csupreme guide\\u201d since 2010. But the Brotherhood\\u2019s mother ship has been decimated since 2013, when a Brotherhood regime popularly elected during the height of the \\u201cArab Spring\\u201d uprising was driven from power by Egypt\\u2019s armed forces after massive popular protests against its repressive governance. The organization has since been outlawed in Egypt, with Badie and other leaders imprisoned. The Brotherhood, moreover, has similarly been banned in Saudi Arabia (formerly, the Brotherhood\\u2019s most important patron), the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, and Jordan, among other Sunni Muslim countries.<\\/p>\\n<p>Yet, at the same time, Brotherhood satellites have embedded themselves in the political systems of various countries of importance to the United States and have at least claimed to forswear the use of force.<\\/p>\\n<p>These countries include, most prominently, our NATO ally, Turkey, and\\u00a0Qatar, which has just been designated a major non-NATO ally. Both countries host U.S. military bases. Such North African governments as Morocco, Tunisia, and Algeria, which our government regards as allies that are cooperative in American anti-terrorism efforts, also maintain that the Brotherhood parties they tolerate are nonviolent.<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-3-desktop\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-large\\" unitType=\\"desktop\\"><\\/AdUnit><MoreFromAuthor desktop=\\"true\\" variant=\\"default\\"><\\/MoreFromAuthor><MoreInTag variant=\\"default\\"><\\/MoreInTag>\\n<p>Thus the dilemma: A sweeping designation of the Brotherhood as a foreign terrorist organization could significantly interfere in relations between our government and cooperative Muslim regimes. But ignoring the Brotherhood would fail to recognize the menace it represents and impede enforcement actions that should be taken against its abettors.<\\/p>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-3-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-3\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<AdUnit name=\\"incontent-4-mobile\\" baseUnitName=\\"incontent-4\\" unitType=\\"mobile\\"><\\/AdUnit>\\n<p>Domestically, the situation is also fraught. The fact is that many prominent Islamist organizations have Brotherhood roots. But to hold up against court challenges, State Department designations have to connect designees to terrorist activity, not just dissent. If, based on nothing more than historic Brotherhood roots, the Justice Department and Treasury took enforcement action against U.S.-based Islamist groups (many of whose members, alas, are American citizens), the result would be endless, frustrating litigation over whether these groups are complicit in violent jihad.<\\/p>\\n<p>Consequently, the administration proposes to focus on subdivisions of the Brotherhood that have been designated as terrorist organizations, to ensure that their component entities and operatives do not evade the enforcement net. The administration also vows to collaborate with governments that are working to eliminate the Brotherhood\\u2019s capabilities and operations. Degrading the organization\\u2019s foreign platforms will promote American national security.<\\/p>\\n<p>If we could turn back time, it would have been better to act against the Brotherhood before it established a foothold in our country 60 years ago. Eradicating it will take work. That begins with recognizing the threat. The administration has taken a good first step.<\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Though it isn\\u2019t a sweeping designation for the entire organization, the administration has taken a good first step.<\\/p>\\n","protected":false},"author":149,"featured_media":1896991,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"hide-more-from-author":false,"disable-player":false,"disable-wfb-100-badge":false,"disable-wfb-100-archive-widget":false,"disable-wfb-100-legacy-widget":false,"hide_top_stories":false,"headline_variations":[],"coral_asset_id":"","_cr_original_post":"","_cr_replace_post_id":"","_cr_replacing_post_id":"","_links_to":"","_links_to_type":0,"original-print-title":"","hide-nrplus":"1","social":{"tweet":"","share-chart":false},"footnotes":""},"categories":[6077,3324],"tags":[7957,3437,2330],"section":[615],"coauthors":[170],"class_list":["post-1896973","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-national-security-defense","category-world","tag-islamism","tag-middle-east","tag-terrorism","section-article"],"share_buttons":{"facebook":{"title":"Share on Facebook","href":"https:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/sharer\\/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Ftrumps-terrorist-designation-of-muslim-brotherhood-sends-right-message%2F"},"twitter":{"title":"Share on Twitter","href":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/intent\\/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Ftrumps-terrorist-designation-of-muslim-brotherhood-sends-right-message%2F&text=Trump%E2%80%99s%20Terrorist%20Designation%20of%20Muslim%20Brotherhood%20Sends%20Right%20Message"},"flipboard":{"title":"Share on Flipboard","href":"https:\\/\\/share.flipboard.com\\/bookmarklet\\/popout?v=2&title=Trump%E2%80%99s%20Terrorist%20Designation%20of%20Muslim%20Brotherhood%20Sends%20Right%20Message&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalreview.com%2F2025%2F11%2Ftrumps-terrorist-designation-of-muslim-brotherhood-sends-right-message%2F&utm_campaign=tools&utm_medium=article-share&utm_source=https:\\/\\/www.nationalreview.com\\/"},"whatsapp":{"title":"Share on WhatsApp","href":"https:\\/\\/wa.me\\/?text=Trump%E2%80%99s%20Terrorist%20Designation%20of%20Muslim%20Brotherhood%20Sends%20Right%20Message%20htt