ctober, said in a statement that it would shut down permanently, having “successfully completed its emergency mission”. International aid organisations refused to work with the GHF, which was launched as famine loomed in Gaza after the total blockade on all supplies imposed by Israel in March.", "articleId": "1fe8f331-49af-4c7a-a2e8-29f91e3f4f09", "articleUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/24/us-and-israel-backed-gaza-humanitarian-foundation-to-end-operations-in-territory", "outletName": "The Guardian", "articleTitle": "US and Israel-backed Gaza Humanitarian Foundation to end operations in territory"}
