 renewable energy sources like wind and solar as more immediate solutions.", "The timeline for nuclear fusion to become a viable energy source remains uncertain, with estimates ranging from a few decades to beyond this century.", "The international community's interest in nuclear fusion reflects a broader search for sustainable and clean energy alternatives to combat climate change."]	{"text": "Germany consumes vast amounts of energy to sustain its manufacturing might and energy-intensive sectors like the automotive and chemical industry. The country, Europe's largest economy, still relies heavily on fossil fuels for its energy needs, even though the share of renewable sources like wind and solar has risen steadily over the past two decades. To balance the energy and environmental commitments, Berlin is also betting on new technologies such as nuclear fusion, which promises abundant, clean, safe, and reliable energy without CO2 emissions.", "articleId": "101474fa-e53a-4cbe-83dd-de07b9b7c3c8", "articleUrl": "https://www.dw.com/en/germany-bets-billions-on-nuclear-fusion-to-secure-clean-energy-future/a-74522109?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-rdf", "outletName": "Deutsche Welle", "articleTitle": "Germany bets billions on nuclear fusion for energy future"}
