 balance between fostering technological innovation and ensuring robust data privacy protections for consumers.", "There is an ongoing discussion about the need for a unified or federal regulatory framework in the United States to effectively compete on the global stage while protecting consumer privacy."]	{"text": "The hundreds of billions of dollars being spent on AI are overwhelming Europe’s commitment to digital privacy and stringent tech regulation. The EU’s AI Act and General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) law are being delayed and weakened, respectively. Former Italian prime minister Mario Draghi had warned a year ago that Europe had fallen behind the US ...", "articleId": "45e2484d-bdda-4fc3-95e6-210a1340d7c5", "articleUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/24/us-europe-artificial-intelligence-ai", "outletName": "The Guardian", "articleTitle": "Europe loosens reins on AI – and US takes them off"}
