ssing both the supply and demand for drugs, emphasizing personal responsibility and recovery.", "The effectiveness of either approach can depend on various factors, including the type of drugs involved, community resources, and the integration of policies into broader social and healthcare systems.", "There is ongoing debate and research into the outcomes of these differing approaches, with some studies suggesting benefits to harm reduction strategies and others highlighting the successes of abstinence-based programs."]	{"text": "At least two major West Coast cities are rethinking their so-called harm reduction policies that have sought to address addiction, signaling that these areas are overhauling their strategy to combat the drug crisis as addiction challenges persist. While cities including San Francisco and Seattle have previously adopted policies to distribute 'safer' drug supplies like clean foil and pipes that could be used to smoke fentanyl or other substances, these cities are now implementing a new approach that imposes new limitations on the distribution of these supplies.", "articleId": "db0a0d8c-310c-428e-8f89-4ef734f81f21", "articleUrl": "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/blue-cities-u-turn-distributing-drug-supplies-addicts-after-progressive-policies-fail-stem-epidemic", "outletName": "Fox News", "articleTitle": "Blue cities U-turn on distributing drug supplies to addicts after progressive policies fail to stem epidemic"}
