y to fall behind in the global AI race.", "Critics of the current trajectory advocate for a balanced approach that ensures AI development is aligned with ethical standards and sustainability goals.", "The debate encompasses a range of perspectives, from those who view deregulation as a necessary step for progress to those who fear it may lead to ethical and environmental oversights."]	{"text": "The hundreds of billions of dollars being spent on AI are overwhelming Europe’s commitment to digital privacy and stringent tech regulation. The EU’s AI Act and General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) law are being delayed and weakened, respectively. Former Italian prime minister Mario Draghi had warned a year ago that Europe had fallen behind the US...", "articleId": "45e2484d-bdda-4fc3-95e6-210a1340d7c5", "articleUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/24/us-europe-artificial-intelligence-ai", "outletName": "The Guardian", "articleTitle": "Europe loosens reins on AI – and US takes them off"}
