 sources are not yet fully developed or integrated.", "Others argue that the focus should be on accelerating the adoption of renewable energy technologies, rather than improving the efficiency of coal plants.", "The debate reflects broader tensions between immediate energy needs and long-term climate goals, with differing views on the best path forward for sustainable energy production.", "Economic considerations, including the cost of AI integration versus the potential savings and profitability from extended coal plant operation, also play a significant role in the debate."]	{"text": "President Donald Trump has amplified those effects by lowering hurdles for fossil fuel development, obstructing renewable energy projects and seeking to erase or weaken regulations that constrained the release of soot, mercury and climate pollution from coal plants. The turnaround is stark: More than 500 coal-fired power plants retired between 2010 and 2019, according to federal data. At the same time, federal regulations reduced the amount of pollution released from the plants. But in the past two years, utilities have delayed the retirements of more than 30 generating units at 15 coal plants across the country to provide power to data centers.", "articleId": "62bd73ee-7dd9-4801-9016-6ee7d60c43ec", "articleUrl": "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/11/27/ai-gives-coal-plants-a-lifeline-as-trump-makes-them-dirtier-00661839", "outletName": "Politico", "articleTitle": "AI gives coal plants a lifeline as Trump makes them dirtier"}
