e amplification of biases.", "Supporters of minimal regulation argue that the rapid evolution of AI technology necessitates a flexible approach to governance, allowing companies to innovate freely.", "The debate reflects broader societal concerns about the balance between innovation and ethical considerations in the development and deployment of AI technologies."]	{"text": "The hundreds of billions of dollars being spent on AI are overwhelming Europe’s commitment to digital privacy and stringent tech regulation. The EU’s AI Act and General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) law are being delayed and weakened, respectively. Former Italian prime minister Mario Draghi had warned a year ago that Europe had fallen behind the US in the digital economy, suggesting a need for a balance between innovation and regulation.", "articleId": "45e2484d-bdda-4fc3-95e6-210a1340d7c5", "articleUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/24/us-europe-artificial-intelligence-ai", "outletName": "The Guardian", "articleTitle": "Europe loosens reins on AI – and US takes them off"}
